    {
      "ordinal": 10,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "3.2",
      "title": "Visor Requirements",
      "body": "● Visor must not be too long or too short, it must respect the proportions of historical sources.\n● The hinge must be reproduced as per historical sources.\n● It is allowed to weld the hinge. Welded hinges must resemble a functional hinge.\n● It is allowed to weld the visor down. Welded visor must resemble a functional removable visor.\n● It is allowed to add a metal plate to protect the throat. Such a plate must be strong enough to endure full contact fight and must be concealed under the aventail.\n● A leather strap can be used to secure the visor down.\n● Breath holes should be round and must not exceed a diameter of 10mm. Breath holes must not be so numerous that they compromise the helm’s structural integrity. It is acceptable to mirror breath holes to both sides.\n● Breath holes of another shape must be documented by historical sources to be allowed.",
      "page_from": 8,
      "page_to": 8,
      "stable_key": "klappvisors:3.2",
      "parent_key": "klappvisors:3",
      "review_status": "extracted",
